todo.py keeps a list of things to do in todo.json, beside the current directory's other files. `python3 todo.py add TEXT` adds one and `python3 todo.py list` prints them, numbered from 1. Add `python3 todo.py done N`, which marks item N done; list then shows a done item with [x] in place of [ ]. `done` with a number that names no item prints an error on standard error and exits with status 1.
